# WIZ YouTube API Configuration Template
# Copy this file to .env.local and add your credentials

# YouTube OAuth Client ID (from Google Cloud Console)
# Format: 123456789-abcdefghijk.googleusercontent.com
VITE_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id-here.googleusercontent.com

# YouTube API Key (from Google Cloud Console) 
# Format: AIzaSyABC123DEF456GHI789...
VITE_YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# Instructions:
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Enable YouTube Data API v3
# 3. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application)
# 4. Add authorized origins: http://localhost:8080 and https://wiz-magic-platform.web.app
# 5. Create API Key (restrict to YouTube Data API v3)
# 6. Copy the credentials above
# 7. Rename this file to .env.local
# 8. Restart your dev server: npm run dev

# After setup, the "OAuth client was not found" error will be fixed!